{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","kind":"response","reasoning":"The repository is empty (only .git). Good — a completely blank slate. Let me write up a short plan.\n\nPlan:\n- Single file: `todo.py` (standard library only: argparse, json, pathlib, sys, and datetime if needed).\n- Storage: `todos.json` next to the script (using `Path(__file__).resolve().parent / \"todos.json\"`), i.e., regardless of cwd, the file sits next to the script.\n- Data model: list of objects: `{\"id\": int, \"text\": str, \"done\": bool, \"created\": str (ISO)}` — or should I omit created to keep it minimal? Keep it minimal: id, text, done. Auto-increment id = max existing + 1.\n- Commands via argparse subparsers:\n  - `add TEXT...` — add a task, print confirmation with id.\n  - `list` — show `[id] text (done)`, mark completed ones with [x], sort by id. If empty, show \"No todos.\"\n  - `done ID` — mark as done; error if id doesn't exist.\n  - (Maybe `undone` too? Not requested — keep it minimal. Skip.)\n- Load/save: `load()` returns [] if file doesn't exist or is empty/corrupt — decision: on corruption, error out with a clear message rather than silently wiping data? Safer: on JSONDecodeError, print an error and exit 1 (don't overwrite). Keep it simple.\n- Atomic-ish write: write to a temp file and replace? For a small tool, simple `json.dump` is enough; but a simple `Path.write_text` is fine too. Keep it minimal: direct write.\n- Exit codes: 0 for success, 1 for errors (unknown id, corrupt file).\n- No dependencies beyond the standard library. Python 3.8+.\n\nTests: run manual smoke tests: add two, list, mark one done, list, verify the JSON file location, error case for `done 99`, behavior when the file doesn't exist.\n\nThen, suggest moving to the build phase with propose_phase_transition.\n","seq":321,"t":43761,"text":"\n\nRepo is empty (just `.git`), so it's a fresh file. Plan:\n\n**File:** single `todo.py` at repo root — stdlib only (`argparse`, `json`, `pathlib`, `sys`).\n\n**Storage:** `todos.json` placed next to the script (`Path(__file__).resolve().parent / \"todos.json\"`), so it works from any cwd. Shape: a JSON list of `{\"id\": int, \"text\": str, \"done\": bool}`. `id` is auto-assigned as `max(existing ids) + 1`.\n\n**Commands** (argparse subparsers):\n- `add TEXT...` — append task, print `[id] added: text`\n- `list` — one line per task: `[id] text` or `[x] text` if done, in id order; prints \"No todos.\" when empty\n- `done ID` — flips `done: true`, prints confirmation; exits 1 with a message if the id doesn't exist\n\n**Error handling:**\n- Missing file → treat as empty list (lazy init)\n- Corrupt JSON → print a clear error, exit 1, never overwrite the file\n- Unknown `done` id → error, exit 1\n- Write-back: plain `json.dump` with indent; no atomic rename needed at this size\n\n**Out of scope (keep it tiny):** no `undone`, no dates, no config.\n\n**What I'd test:** fresh-run `add` twice → `list` → `done 1` → `list` (shows `[x]`), confirm `todos.json` sits next to the script and survives a run from another directory, `done 99` → exit 1, corrupt-JSON case → error without data loss.\n\n","timings":{"cache_n":2560,"draft_n":2023,"draft_n_accepted":633,"predicted_ms":10090.0,"predicted_n":922,"prompt_ms":460.0,"prompt_n":382},"to_request":48,"usage":{"cached_tokens":2560,"completion_tokens":922,"prompt_tokens":2942}}
