anted to record?\" — this is an invitation. A concise, useful entry: smoke test steps 1–5 passed (add/list/done work, done tasks show as [x]); step 6 (done 99 → expect exit 1) is pending, and I'll run it now. That fits \"evidence\" or \"latest\". I'll record one concise entry.\n\nLet me make the update_record call and the first bash call. The update_record is independent of the bash calls, so it can be batched... but wait, should I run (6) first? The user asked to run (7) and (8). I'll run (6) because it's part of the smoke test and hasn't been run yet. Let me briefly state this in my reply.\n\nTool calls: one command per tool call. So sequential bash calls. The update_record can be batched with the first bash call (independent).\n\nLet's do it: update_record + bash(done 99) in one block. Then cat todo.json. Then list. Then add third task (e.g., \"add water plants\"). Then list.\n","seq":1079,"t":766261,"text":"","timings":{"cache_n":6400,"draft_n":1953,"draft_n_accepted":631,"predicted_ms":9980.0,"predicted_n":910,"prompt_ms":290.0,"prompt_n":149},"to_request":820,"usage":{"cached_tokens":6400,"completion_tokens":910,"prompt_tokens":6549}}
